ed `enrich: bool = False` parameter to `extract_supplemental()` and `_route_by_content_class()`\n- `phase2_extract.py` now passes `config.supplemental_material.enrich_with_searches` to `extract_supplemental(enrich=...)`\n\n#### 7. Filestore Path Consolidation\n- Source maps (`maps.py`) defaulted to `output/maps_images/` — NOT in filestore\n- Added `image_storage_path: \"filestore/maps/\"` to `maps:` section in `config.yaml`\n- All download paths now route to `filestore/`: equipment→`filestore/equipment/`, external maps→`filestore/external_maps/`, source maps→`filestore/maps/`\n\n### Previous Sessions (Carried Forward)\n- Supplemental split architecture (bibliography + factual content + ambiguous routing)\n- `alt_title` field for expanded abbreviations in citations\n- ULID fixing wired into ALL extractors\n- JSON schema validation for casualties and people_groups\n- `scripts/validate_output.py` comprehensive output validator (5140/5141 valid)\n- Equipment `country_of_origin`, generic name rejection\n- Phase 3 enrichment bug fix\n\n## TECHNICAL CONTEXT\n\n### Batch Extraction Pattern\nThe existing `batch_parallel.py` `_batch_extract()` sends all sub-events in one prompt for dates/places/people/groups (5 calls per chapter instead of 5×N). The same pattern is being applied to weather/logistics/casualties.\n\n**Key difference:** The optional extractors (weather/logistics/casualties) need entity indices for post-processing (linking to dates, places, people, equipment). The batch call only replaces the Grok API call — all post-processing remains per-item.\n\n### Casualties Batch — Current State of Code\nFile: `src/extraction/casualties.py`\n\nNew function `_batch_extract_casualties()` (inserted before `_extract_from_event`):\n- Filters sub-events using `_has_casualty_mention()` \n- Builds single prompt with all relevant sub-events: `--- Sub-event [<ID>] ---\\n<text>`\n- Asks for JSON dict keyed by sub-event ID: `{\"<Sub-eventID>\": [<casualty items>], ...}`\n- Parses response, runs `_fix_invalid_ulids` + `_validate_items` per sub-event\n- Returns `Dict[str, List[Dict]]`\n\nModified `extract_casualties()`:\n- Calls `_batch_extract_casualties()` once\n- Loops over sub-events, looks up results by ID\n- Calls existing `_build_casualty()` for each item (entity linking preserved)\n- **Note:** The old code also processed the main event (not just sub-events). The new code only processes sub-events. Need to verify if main event processing is needed.\n\n### Logistics Batch — Current State of Code\nFile: `src/extraction/logistics.py`\n\nNew functions:\n- `_get_sub_event_text()` — extracts text from sub-event (handles both `text` and `Sub-event_fulltext` dict)\n- `_batch_extract_logistics()` — similar pattern to casualties batch, uses `extract_json` instead of `extract_structured`, validates with `LogisticsExtraction.model_validate()`\n\nModified `extract_logistics_from_event()`:\n- Calls `_batch_extract_logistics()` once\n- Loops over sub-events, looks up results by ID\n- Rest of processing (entity linking, file saving) unchanged\n\n### Weather Batch — NOT YET IMPLEMENTED\nFile: `src/extraction/weather_central.py`\n\n**Complexity:** Each sub-event prompt includes place/date context via `_build_places_section()` and `_build_dates_section()`. These reference `sub_event[\"Places\"]` and `sub_event[\"Dates\"]` arrays with PlaceMentionIDs and DateMentionIDs.\n\n**Approach needed:** Include place/date context per sub-event in the batch prompt. The response structure needs `Weather_Mentions` keyed by sub-event ID. Post-processing (`_find_or_create_weather`, `_add_event_mention`, optional API fetch) stays per-mention.\n\nKey functions in weather flow:\n- `create_weather_prompt()` — builds per-sub-event prompt with place/date sections\n- `_extract_weather_for_sub_event()` — calls `extract_structured(schema=WeatherOutput)`, processes mentions\n- `extract_weather_central()` — loops over sub-events, calls above function\n- `WeatherOutput` Pydantic model with `Weather_Mentions` array\n- `WeatherMention` fields: WeatherMentionID, place_name, PlaceMentionID, date, DateMentionID, weather_description, temperature, etc.\n\n### API Call Distribution (from cache analysis)\n```\nBatch core (events/dates/places/people/groups): 929 calls (18%)\nWeather: 1,204 calls (24%) — TARGET FOR BATCHING\nLogistics: 1,134 calls (22%) — TARGET FOR BATCHING  \nCasualties: 469 calls (9%) — TARGET FOR BATCHING\nEquipment extraction: 198 (4%)\nEquipment enrichment+media: 580 (12%)\nSupplemental search: 532 (11%)\nTOTAL: ~5,058 calls → ~2,519 after batching (50% reduction)\n```\n\n### Validation Coverage Matrix\n| Extractor | ULID Fix | Schema Validation | Method |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| events.py | ✅ | ✅ | JSON Schema (`EVENT_SCHEMA`) |\n| supplemental.py | ✅ | ✅ | JSON Schema (`SUPPLEMENTAL_SCHEMA`) |\n| dates.py | ✅ | ✅ | Pydantic (`extract_structured`) |\n| places.py | ✅ | ✅ | Pydantic (`extract_structured`) |\n| people.py | ✅ | ✅ | Pydantic (`extract_structured`) |\n| weather_central.py | ✅ | ✅ | Pydantic (`extract_structured`) |\n| logistics.py | N/A | ✅ | Pydantic (`extract_structured` + `model_validate`) |\n| equipment.py | ✅ | ✅ | Pydantic (`model_validate`) |\n| casualties.py | ✅ | ✅ | JSON Schema (`CASUALTY_ITEM_SCHEMA`) per item |\n| people_groups.py | ✅ | ✅ | JSON Schema (`PEOPLE_GROUP_ITEM_SCHEMA`) per item |\n| batch_parallel.py | ✅ | — | Minimal keys; full extractors validate downstream |\n\n### Key Config State (`config.yaml`)\n```yaml\nmaps:\n  image_storage_path: \"filestore/maps/\"  # NEW — was defaulting to output/maps_images\nexternal_maps:\n  image_storage_path: \"filestore/external_maps/\"\nsupplemental_material:\n  enabled: true\n  enrich_with_searches: true  # Now wired to extract_supplemental(enrich=True)\n```\n\n### Known Data Issue\n`output/people_groups/3ad.json` — broken file, missing GroupID and name fields.\n\n### Output directory\n`output/` was cleaned (empty) during this session. No output data files exist currently.\n\n## TOOLS EXECUTED\n\n### File Modifications (This Session)\n- `src/extraction/casualties.py` — Added `_batch_extract_casualties()`, modified `extract_casualties()` to use batch\n- `src/extraction/logistics.py` — Added `_get_sub_event_text()`, `_batch_extract_logistics()`, modified `extract_logistics_from_event()` to use batch\n- `src/extraction/supplemental.py` — Added `enrich` param to `extract_supplemental()` and `_route_by_content_class()`, wired `_enrich_material()` call\n- `phase2_extract.py` — Passes `enrich_with_searches` config to `extract_supplemental()`\n- `config.yaml` — Added `image_storage_path: \"filestore/maps/\"` to maps section\n- `scripts/validate_output.py` — Extracted `_validate_entity_dirs()` and `_collect_entity_files()` from `main()`\n- 10 documentation files updated, 3 archived\n- `src/json_schemas.py` — Added `alt_title`, `content_class` to SUPPLEMENTAL_SCHEMA\n\n### Compilation Verified\n- `src/extraction/supplemental.py` ✅\n- `phase2_extract.py` ✅\n- `scripts/validate_output.py` ✅\n- **casualties.py and logistics.py NOT YET COMPILED/TESTED**\n\n### QA Completed\n- Black: ✅ all changed files\n- Radon: validate_output.py main() C(13)→A(5); no C-rated functions remain\n- Bandit: 2 pre-existing low-severity findings (equipment.py only)\n- Vulture: all findings pre-existing (Pydantic fields, entry-point functions)\n- Pylint: 9.30/10 overall (pre-existing equipment.py issues)\n\n## NEXT STEPS\n\n1. **Compile and test casualties.py and logistics.py** — `py_compile` both files, verify no syntax errors\n2. **Verify casualties batch handles main event** — Old code processed main event AND sub-events; new code only processes sub-events. Check if main event processing is needed (it may have description text with casualties)\n3. **Implement weather batch** — Most complex of the three:\n   - Build batch prompt that includes per-sub-event place/date context\n   - Use `extract_json` instead of `extract_structured` for batch call\n   - Validate each mention against WeatherMention fields\n   - Keep `_find_or_create_weather`, `_add_event_mention`, API fetch per-mention\n4. **Run QA on all three modified extractors** — Black, pylint, radon, py_compile\n5. **Test full pipeline** — Run phase2 on a chapter to verify batch extractors produce same output format\n6. **Wire `supplemental_advanced.py` to `output/bibliography/`** — Phase 3 enrichment still reads from old location\n7. **Fix `3ad.json`** — Broken people_group file\n\n## TODO LIST\nID if loaded: none\n\nActive TODOs from `docs/current/TODO.md`:\n- Wire `supplemental_advanced.py` to `output/bibliography/` (Medium)\n- Fix `output/people_groups/3ad.json` (Low)\n- Windows PowerShell script equivalents (Medium)\n- Batch weather/logistics/casualties (IN PROGRESS — casualties and logistics code written, weather not started)\n\n## FACTUAL RECORD\n\n### Files Modified and Read\n_(Most frequently and recently accessed first. Indented items show summaries for the last 5 modifications.)_\n* /Users/dchristian/projects/SecondWorldWarAsData/src/extraction/supplemental.py (3 modifications, 12 reads)\n  - Wire enrichment into _route_by_content_class for document_reference only\n  - Add enrich parameter to extract_supplemental\n  - Pass grok_client and enrich flag to _route_by_content_class\n* /Users/dchristian/projects/SecondWorldWarAsData/src/extraction/casualties.py (2 modifications, 7 reads)\n  - Replace per-sub-event loop with batch extraction call\n  - Add _batch_extract_casualties function\n* /Users/dchristian/projects/SecondWorldWarAsData/docs/current/INDEX.md (5 modifications, 1 read)\n  - Add design doc link and update supplemental section in index\n  - Update reference section with schema reference note\n  - Update last updated date\n  - Update header date\n  - Update footer date\n* /Users/dchristian/projects/SecondWorldWarAsDa...eatures/supplemental/SUPPLEMENTAL_COMPLETE.md (5 modifications, 1 read)\n  - Rewrite supplemental complete doc to reflect split archite